ings and provide a clear price before repair work starts. The proposed work depends on the fault, the parts required and access to the equipment. All jobs come with warranty; ask for the applicable coverage when agreeing the repair.</p><p>For a restaurant in Camden, a grocery shop in Islington or a café in Westminster, the immediate concern is keeping service organised while refrigeration is assessed. Our emergency contact line is available around the clock, and attendance timing is discussed when you call with your London postcode. We also cover businesses in Hackney, Barnet, Ealing and surrounding districts. Before the visit, make the cabinet accessible and note any recent maintenance, unusual sounds or error messages. Follow your business&#x27;s food safety procedures for affected stock. Call 07983 759320 to discuss the breakdown, or use the booking enquiry link with the fridge details and your preferred contact number.</p><h3>Fridge faults and symptoms we investigate</h3><ul><li>Thermostat and temperature sensor faults: inaccurate readings or erratic switching can leave a cabinet cycling too frequently or failing to call for cooling when needed.</li><li>Compressor starting problems: repeated clicking, protective trips or prolonged running require diagnosis of the starting components and operating conditions before a replacement decision is made.</li><li>Door seal damage: split gaskets, loose hinges and poor alignment allow warm kitchen air into the cabinet, increasing condensation and making temperature recovery more difficult.</li><li>Refrigerant leaks: reduced cooling may need leak investigation and an assessment of the sealed system. Adding refrigerant alone does not resolve the source of a leak.</li><li>Fan motor failures: a stopped or noisy evaporator fan can leave shelves at different temperatures, while condenser airflow problems can make the equipment struggle under load.</li><li>Drainage and airflow restrictions: water beneath the cabinet or ice around 